            <ArticleTitle>Bilateral thoracotomy and inferior sternotomy for bypass grafting after esophagostomy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>847-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In the presence of a cervical esophagostomy, a median sternotomy may jeopardize the stoma, risk mediastinal or sternal infection, and potentially compromise future esophageal operations. Coronary artery bypass grafting was performed using a modified bilateral thoracotomy before esophageal reconstruction in a patient with cervical esophagostomy. The surgical technique is described with a review of the relevant literature.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
